# Board-specific init
boards/Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.scm

# Serial file+command tunnel: resident LLIP receiver -- host sends (llt) then op/da/cl file
# frames and/or (ev <form>) command frames; O(N) clean, no per-char REPL echo.
features/llip-serial.scm

# P123 Part D: carry a camera frame over LLIP as BINARY (s-expression header + raw bytes).
# NOT base64 -- every LambLisp port is already a binary port, so a JPEG rides the same TCP
# connection the move programs use, unencoded.  Codec only: it loads on a board with no camera.
features/llip-vision.scm

# LLIP SERVER -- filesystem operations for a remote LambLisp client.  Added 2026-09-12: EVERY
# PUBLISHED TARGET SUPPORTS LLIP BY DEFAULT.  This target staged the serial RECEIVER below but not
# the SERVER, so `llip ls/send/run` against it answered nothing -- a capability the customer's own
# `tools/llip` CLI advertises, shipped half-present.  The two halves are not interchangeable:
# llip-serial.scm is the resident (llt) that accepts a serial session; llip-server.scm is what
# serves the file operations inside it.
tools/llip-server.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
# Peer CA for the `network` test_id: written by _w3_run_network, absent otherwise (untracked).
optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem -> net-test-ca.pem
# Bench WiFi credentials: untracked, absent by default, silent when absent (see .example).
#
# RE-STAGED 2026-09-16 -- B411's exposure is FIXED, and this line is un-commented on the strength
# of the exit condition the previous note wrote for itself: "If someone flashes it and it boots fine
# with the override staged, say so and revert this."  It was flashed, the override was staged, and
# it boots fine.  Measured on THIS board rather than predicted from the 4WD:
#
#     [fastram] wifi reserved 49152                 <- claimed at installer time, pool still whole
#     [fastram] wifi released 49152 to its consumer <- handed over at WiFi.begin()
#     [heap] load d1 WiFi.scm  INT 36008 -> 39572 (+3564) | largest 14324 -> 36852
#     uptime 0:00:30.951  loops 10906  loops/sec 440.40   -- ONE reset in the capture, no loop
#
# WHY IT NOW FITS, and it is ordering rather than slack: the radio's claim is made in
# WiFi_install_mop3 while the largest contiguous block is still 61,428, instead of scavenging
# whatever the .scm chain has left at 26,612.  See [P211] and src/ll_fastram.h.  The second half is
# [31d01dc], which moved ~1,600 interned symbol names to PSRAM and took this board from 3,364 bytes
# free at boot to 57,624.  B411's original mechanism was real -- the allocation that failed was the
# mutex uart_write needs, so the abort could not report itself -- it simply no longer triggers.
#
# THE 4WD IS NOT COVERED BY THIS.  Same SoC, same budget, but it was not re-tested and its manifest
# still comments this line out.  Do NOT un-comment it there on the strength of this measurement:
# that is exactly the predicted-from-a-sibling reasoning this note is replacing.
#
# THE COST IS REAL AND VISIBLE: with the radio up, `[ncg] exec_pool_init: internal alloc 32768
# failed` -- there is not room for both the radio and the 32 KB native pool on a 320 KB part with no
# PSRAM-execute.  That is now the SYSTEM's choice made first, rather than an accident of call order,
# and it matches the standing rule that LX6 stays on bytecode except for purposeful compilations.
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite -- the perf and GC-pause benches, matching the S3 and C5 manifests.
# B455: THESE WERE ABSENT, AND THE MATRIX DID NOT KNOW.  `_W3_PERF_LX6` defaults to this board and
# the registry carries T073 (perf-embedded) and T121 (gcpause) as `enabled`, so the harness has been
# willing to run both here all along -- against a filesystem with no benchmark on it.  Measured
# 2026-09-17: `w3 test perf-embedded LL WROVER` ran 90 minutes, walked 24 indices and produced ZERO
# timing rows, because every boot reported
#     LL_File_System::open() failed to open ll_tests/bench-runner.scm mode r
# and neither harness stop rule could fire (the end-of-suite sentinel is printed BY the missing
# file, and a "miss" was counted only when a board answered NOTHING -- this one chattered).
# FLASH IS NOT THE REASON THEY WERE OMITTED, which was the first thing checked: storage here is
# 512 KB (partitions_4M_ota.csv) and the staged image is 148 KB, so both benches take it to 210 KB,
# 40% of the partition.  B65's FS-overflow was the 4WD at 284 KB on a smaller layout, not this.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm   -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm     -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
